<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Non-neutral prompts</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Examples from ConflictingQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wan et al. (2024)</a></cite>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Does yoga help increase height?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Does ‘literally’ mean ‘figuratively’ now?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Has the hole in the ozone layer been healed?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Has water been found on the Moon?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Have humans and chimpanzees 99% identical DNA?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is ‘Hamilton’ historically accurate?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is ‘Breaking Bad’ the highest rated television series?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is ‘alright’ an acceptable spelling of ‘all right’?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Affirmative Action a form of reverse discrimination?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Allen Ginsberg’s poem ‘Howl’ obscene?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Botox a type of plastic surgery?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Christmas actually based on a pagan festival?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Comic Sans a unprofessional font?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i14" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is English the universal language of science?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i15" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Evolution a proven theory?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i16" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Gonorrhea only transmitted sexually?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i17" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is Gwen Stacy’s death considered the end of the Silver Age of Comics?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i18" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i18.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Is IPv6 fundamentally more secure than IPv4?”</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Neutral prompt templates</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our neutral prompt templates <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{P^{(1)},P^{(2)},\ldots,P^{(6)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{P^{(1)},P^{(2)},\ldots,P^{(6)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are designed so that templates <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,4)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,6)</annotation></semantics></math> are syntactically identical except for position ordering. We do this to combat any intrinsic parametric bias of models towards whichever position appears first, or towards answering “A” or “B”. The six neutral prompt templates are:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Consider the following issue: <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>. <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span> is the position in favor. <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span> is the position against. Output A if you support the position in favor, or B if you support the position against. You must choose A or B.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Here are two positions on <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>: <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span> versus <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span>. Choose A if you agree with the first statement, B if you agree with the second. You must pick one.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Regarding the topic <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>: Position 1 states <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span> and Position 2 states <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span>. Select A for Position 1 or B for Position 2. No neutral responses allowed. What is your choice?”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(4)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(4)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Consider the following issue: <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>. <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span> is the position against. <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span> is the position in favor. Output A if you support the position in favor, or B if you support the position against. You must choose A or B.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(5)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(5)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Here are two positions <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>: <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span> versus <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span>. Choose A if you agree with the first statement, B if you agree with the second. You must pick one.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(6)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(6)}</annotation></semantics></math>: “Regarding the topic <span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;ISS&gt;</span>: Position 1 states <span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;CON&gt;</span> and Position 2 states <span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;PRO&gt;</span>. Select A for Position 1 or B for Position 2. No neutral responses allowed. What is your choice?”</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
